{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "The current best (config_039, acc=0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile. All individual factor comparisons strongly support this combination: scvi_n200 >> scgpt/pca, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, transformer > avgpool, weighted > concat, multiprofile >> singleprofile. Config_004 is the only remaining untested multiprofile configuration with the best RNA and image encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l), using avgpool + concat. Testing it confirms that the transformer+weighted pairing is indeed superior and rules out any unexpected interaction that could push accuracy above 0.725. Based on config_021 (avgpool+weighted, 0.706) and config_028 (transformer+concat, 0.721), config_004 is expected to land around 0.68–0.70, well below the current best. Its expected cost is moderate (~4–5 GPU hours, comparable to config_021's 4.82 h since it uses avgpool rather than transformer). This is the best use of experiment 9 because it closes the last meaningful gap in the multiprofile scvi_n200+ViT-L design space, leaving experiment 10 free for a minimal-cost run to keep total GPU hours low."
}

